Employee App Phase E — high-value additions


-- Request Leave: balance --
PASS  balance display is gated on the server's balances_enabled flag
PASS  only fields the API actually emits are read
PASS  the phantom fields that produced a fake zero are gone from the contract
PASS  no screen still reads balance_days
PASS  a missing number is never coerced to zero
PASS  non-numeric values are refused rather than cast
PASS  Request Leave reads the balance through the shared accessor
PASS  the balance shown is for the leave type being requested, not the first row
PASS  Request Leave reuses the Leave tab's query key rather than a second fetch path
PASS  balances are labelled as information while the server calls them non-binding
PASS  eligibility date is surfaced when the balance cannot yet be taken

-- Request Leave: requested duration --
PASS  duration is fetched from the server
PASS  the request is keyed on the exact selection so a stale count cannot show
PASS  the count is only rendered when the server says it is available
PASS  there is no local day-count fallback anywhere in the request flow
PASS  the copy says working days, matching what the server computes
PASS  a range with no working days says so instead of showing 0
PASS  duration failures are not retried into an error state

-- Profile: manager contact --
PASS  the manager's name is shown when the roster has one
PASS  the contact action appears only when the stored number is dialable
PASS  an unrecognised number produces no action rather than a bad tel: link
PASS  dialling is a discrete control, not the whole row
PASS  the call target meets the touch-target floor
PASS  a device that cannot dial fails quietly
PASS  no chat, messaging or third-party contact channel was introduced
PASS  no manager contact field beyond what /app/profile returns is read

-- Inbox: relative time --
PASS  rows show relative time
PASS  the exact timestamp is preserved for assistive technology
PASS  the exact timestamp is rendered in Kuwait time
PASS  relative-time key time.justNow exists in EN and AR
PASS  relative-time key time.minutesAgo exists in EN and AR
PASS  relative-time key time.hoursAgo exists in EN and AR
PASS  relative-time key time.yesterday exists in EN and AR
PASS  older messages fall back to a localized date rather than a growing day count

-- Payslips: year grouping --
PASS  history is grouped by year
PASS  only the most recent year opens on arrival
PASS  a lone year cannot be collapsed into an empty screen
PASS  a non-collapsible group always renders its rows
PASS  each year is paged rather than rendered whole
PASS  net pay keeps its prominence
PASS  no search or filter chrome was added for a 12-per-year dataset
PASS  documents history gets the same single-year treatment

-- Home: document expiry task --
PASS  the task detail rides on the server projection, not a second Home fetch
PASS  Home does not re-query the documents module
PASS  the day count is derived from the server's expiry date
PASS  the document is named with the module's own label
PASS  no detail means the generic label, never an implied urgency
PASS  an unparseable expiry falls back rather than rendering a wrong count
PASS  already-expired and expiring-today are stated correctly, not as negative days
PASS  the expiry copy exists in both locales
PASS  empty detail fields cannot masquerade as present
PASS  the task still routes to Documents
PASS  no permanent expiry dashboard or new compliance surface was added

